<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rudamun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rudamun was the last king of the Theban line known as the Twenty-third Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, reigning briefly in the 8th century BCE. A younger son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osorkon-iii">Osorkon III</a>, he succeeded his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takelot-iii">Takelot III</a>. After his reign his family's power declined to local rule, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a> passed under the influence of the Kushite kings and their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gods-wife-of-amun">God's Wife of Amun</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rudamun.jpg" alt="Rudamun" width="320" height="592" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aoineko · CC BY-SA 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egypte_louvre_054.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
